<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH PHILIP MORRIS UNIT 96 NET PROFIT FALLS.</title>
<headline>CZECH PHILIP MORRIS UNIT 96 NET PROFIT FALLS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech cigarette maker Tabak a.s., majority owned by Philip Morris Co, said on Wednesday its net profit dipped to 1.6 billion crowns in 1996 from 1.8 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>The firm said in a published statement that gross profit fell to 2.3 billion last year from 1995's 3.1 billion.  </p>
<p>Results for year ending December 31, 1996 (in millions of</p>
<p>crowns):</p>
<p> Net profit	   1,600.80     vs	 1,805.22</p>
<p> Gross profit	 2,330.55     vs	 3,077.15</p>
<p> Total revenues    10,676.79     vs	 9,849.47</p>
<p> Total assets	10,891.33     vs	11,098.79</p>
<p>Note. The company is listed on the free market of the</p>
<p>Prague Stock Exchange. Philip Morris Co holds a 68 percent</p>
<p>stake in Tabak, based in Kutna Hora, 75 km east of Prague.</p>
<p>Tabak said in the statement that its annual meeting would</p>
<p>take place on May 23.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
